{{!-- What Stonetop has built that changes how a STEP of the season works.

      "When you consume Surplus in winter, consider Population to be 1 lower." "Consumes 1 less
      Surplus than normal." "Roll 2d6+Population instead of 1d4+Population." Five improvements bend
      winter's consumption, and every one of them used to sit in the same undifferentiated wall as
      the results that simply add Surplus — nowhere near the place Surplus is actually consumed,
      because there was no consumption step in the UI to put them beside.

      Headed by the STEP, so the heading states when they apply and no row has to. Never a control:
      an adjustment changes an arithmetic the sheet does not perform.

      Params: statement (TurnoverStatement). --}}
{{#if statement.adjustmentGroups.length}}
	<div class="steading-adjustments">
		{{#each statement.adjustmentGroups}}
			<h5 class="steading-adjustments-head">{{localize labelKey}}</h5>
			<ul class="steading-statement-lines steading-statement-lines--sourced stonetop-unmarked">
				{{#each lines}}
					<li class="steading-statement-line">
						<span class="steading-statement-source">{{source}}</span>
						<span class="steading-statement-clause">{{rich text}}</span>
					</li>
				{{/each}}
			</ul>
		{{/each}}
	</div>
{{/if}}
